    "body": "## Motivation\n\nThe NPU AWQ linear fallback always casts dequantized weights to BF16, including when scales and activations are FP16. This discards FP16 precision before the linear operation. For example, with local K = group size = 128, an FP16 scale of 0.10028076171875 produces 12.8125 instead of 12.8359375 for an all-one input.\n\n## Modifications\n\nCast fallback weights to `layer.scales.dtype`. The quantized matmul fast path is unchanged.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nRan the original and patched loader and linear methods on an NPU with torch-npu 2.10.0.post6:\n\n- 36 cases: K/group size 64/64 and 128/128 (fallback), 256/128 (fast-path control); FP16/BF16; bias/no bias; constant and random weights, asymmetric zeros, 2D/3D inputs.\n- Before: 24 passed, 12 failed. All failures were FP16 fallback cases.\n- After: 36 passed. Fallback weights and outputs match the independently unpacked, dtype-preserving dense reference exactly. Fast-path controls use rtol=0.02, atol=0.125.\n- The example above now returns 12.8359375.\n\nThe harness executes the class extracted from each source file. These are operator-level checks, not a full-model accuracy evaluation.\n\n![NPU validation results](https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/AkiYangDev/sglang@b235e8fc9b919aa44c4fe325a7afa67c3e7990e0/validation.png)\n\n[Raw results](https://github.com/AkiYangDev/sglang/blob/b235e8fc9b919aa44c4fe325a7afa67c3e7990e0/RESULT.json)\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNot run.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Formatting and applicable lint checks passed. Two hooks requiring `python3` on Windows were run directly with the installed Python.\n- [x] NPU correctness checks completed.\n- [ ] Full-model accuracy and performance benchmarks.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #41192619026](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41192619026)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #41192618863](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41192618863)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #41192618824](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41192618824)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
